{"run_id":"session_refresh_replay_01|agentic:crg|0","task_id":"session_refresh_replay_01","condition":"agentic:crg","backend":"claude-code","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","repeat":0,"diagnosis":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","symbol":"SessionRelationalRepository.updateByHash","start_line":63,"end_line":83,"explanation":"updateByHash ignores conditions.hash. It updates by id only (`{ id: Number(conditions.id) }`), so the refresh token's hash is never compared to the session's current hash. A rotated (old) refresh token still has a valid signature and session id, so the update succeeds again and a new token pair is issued. The document (Mongo) repository filters on both _id and hash, which is the correct behaviour."}],"fix":{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","description":"Include the hash in the update condition: `this.sessionRepository.update({ id: Number(conditions.id), hash: conditions.hash }, { hash: payload.hash })`. Then a stale hash affects 0 rows and the method returns null, so refreshToken throws UnauthorizedException. Also fetch the entity by id after the update.","replacement_code":"const result = await this.sessionRepository.update(\n  { id: Number(conditions.id), hash: conditions.hash },\n  { hash: payload.hash },\n);"}},"usage":{"input":10,"output":1378,"cache_read":80277,"cache_write":6857},"usage_source":"api-reported","cost_usd":0.049255700000000006,"latency_ms":14733,"turns":9,"tool_calls":{"Grep":3,"Read":4},"retrieval_calls":0,"stop_reason":"submitted","transcript_path":"/home/adityareddy/dev/experiments/code-graphs/experiments/02-agent-diagnosis/results/stage1-agentic-dev/transcripts/session_refresh_replay_01_agentic_crg_0.jsonl","workspace_hash":"6a7bde734d15fe8bb74324f81c40e6b26c1f9cad6012668c19c5f2a200397dcc","prompt_version":"p1","profile":"restricted-oauth","workspace_modified":false,"permission_denials":0,"